[mali-g2] Hooks for the persistent implicit pipeline cache (mali-g2/vortek/src/pipeline_cache.c).

DXVK passes no VkPipelineCache and the Mali driver keeps no shader cache of its own, so every game
start compiled every pipeline again (~15 ms for a material-sized shader on the Mali-G2, ~0.2 ms
from a cache). The connection remembers VkApplicationInfo.pApplicationName; vkCreateDevice gives the
device a VkPipelineCache loaded from <VORTEK_PIPELINE_CACHE_DIR>/<application>.<driver key>.vkpc;
pipeline creation uses it when the application passes none (not for plain GPL fast links) and
reports counts and times; releasing a device (vkDestroyDevice, or the cleanup after a client that is
gone) saves what is new and destroys the cache. Test: tests/pcache_test.sh.

